<sect1 id="gamemode" xreflabel="GameMode-&gamemode-version;">
  <?dbhtml filename="gamemode.html" ?>

  <title>GameMode-&gamemode-version;</title>

  <indexterm zone="gamemode">
    <primary sortas="a-gamemode">GameMode</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <sect2 role="package">
    <title>Introduction to GameMode</title>

    <para>
      The GameMode package provides a daemon, utilities, and libraries which
      allows games to request optimizations which then get applied to the host
      temporarily.
    </para>

    &meson-cross;

    <itemizedlist spacing="compact">
      <listitem>
        <para>
          Download: <ulink url="&gamemode-download;"/>
        </para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>

    <bridgehead renderas="sect3">GameMode Dependencies</bridgehead>

    <para role="required">
      <xref linkend="dbus"/>
    </para>

    <para role="recommended">
      <xref linkend="inih"/>,
      &logind;, and
      <xref linkend="polkit"/> (for the daemon)
    </para>

    <para role="optional">
      <ulink url="&blfs-svn;/general/appstream.html">AppStream</ulink>
    </para>

  </sect2>

  <sect2 role="installation">
    <title>Installation of GameMode</title>

    <para>
      Install GameMode by running the following commands:
    </para>

<screen><userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=/usr                      \
            --libexecdir=/usr/libexec/gamemode \
            --buildtype=release                \</userinput><userinput revision="openrc,sysv">
            -D with-sd-bus-provider=elogind    \</userinput><userinput>
            .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</userinput></screen>

    <para>
      Now, as the &root; user:
    </para>

<screen role="root"><userinput>ninja install</userinput></screen>

    <para revision="systemd">
      If you installed the recommended dependencies and haven't installed this
      package just as a dependency, enable the daemon for every user as the
      &root; user:
    </para>

<screen role="root"
  revision="systemd"><userinput>systemctl enable --global gamemoded</userinput></screen>

  </sect2>

  <sect2 role="installation">
    <title>lib32 Installation of GameMode</title>

    <para>
      Install lib32-GameMode by running the following commands:
    </para>

<screen><userinput>rm -rf * &amp;&amp;
meson setup --prefix=/usr                     \
            --buildtype=release               \
            --cross-file=lib32                \
            -D with-sd-bus-provider=no-daemon \
            .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</userinput></screen>

    <para>
      Now, as the &root; user:
    </para>

<screen role="root"><userinput>DESTDIR=$PWD/DESTDIR ninja install    &amp;&amp;
cp -vR DESTDIR/usr/lib32/* /usr/lib32 &amp;&amp;
rm -rf DESTDIR                        &amp;&amp;
ldconfig</userinput></screen>

  </sect2>

  <sect2 role="commands">
    <title>Command Explanations</title>

    &options-meson;

    <para><parameter>--libexecdir=/usr/libexec/gamemode</parameter>: This
    parameter ensures there are no binary conflicts in <filename
    class="directory">/usr/libexec</filename>.</para>

    &meson-buildtype-release;

    <para revision="openrc,sysv"><parameter>-D with-sd-bus-provider=elogind</parameter>:
    This parameter ensures that elogind gets used instead of systemd-logind,
    as Systemd is the default in this package. You can override the requirement
    for logind altogether via the next parameter.</para>

    <para><parameter>-D with-sd-bus-provider=no-daemon</parameter>: This
    parameter disables building the daemon which requires &logind; and
    inih. This is used in the lib32 build since the daemon doesn't provide any
    libraries.</para>

  </sect2>

  <sect2 revision="openrc" id="gamemode-init">
    <title>OpenRC Service</title>

    <para>
      To automatically start the <command>gamemoded</command> daemon when the
      system is rebooted, install and the OpenRC service:
    </para>

<screen role="root"><userinput>&install-exec; /dev/stdin /etc/user/init.d/gamemoded &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<literal>#!/sbin/openrc-run
# Starts the gamemoded daemon
# Authors: Zeckma - zeckma@linuxfromscratch.com
# Version: LFS &version;

description="starts the gamemoded daemon"

supervisor=supervise-daemon
command_background=yes
command="/usr/bin/gamemoded"</literal>
EOF</userinput></screen>
    <para>
      As a regular user, enable the service:
    </para>
<screen><userinput>&rc-user-add; gamemoded default</userinput></screen>
  </sect2>

